<title>LEBANON: All Lebanese t-bill yields fall.</title>
<headline>All Lebanese t-bill yields fall.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>All yields fell on Lebanese treasury bills, according to weekly rates issued by the Bank of Lebanon on Monday.</p>
<p>It announced the following interest rates for its December 19 issues (previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term		     Discount		     Yield</p>
<p>				(percent)		   (percent)</p>
<p>    Three months	  13.78 (13.80)	     14.27 (14.29)</p>
<p>    Six months	    14.93 (14.95)	     16.13 (16.15)</p>
<p>    12 months	     14.46 (14.55)	     16.90 (17.02)</p>
<p>    24 months   (Interest payable twice yearly) 19.28 (19.58)</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 864148 602057 645456</p>
</text>
